<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erispoe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 857</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erispoe was ruler of Brittany from 851 to 857, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a>. Soon after succeeding his father he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jengland">Battle of Jengland</a> in 851, and the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Angers</a> that followed recognised him as king, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pays-de-retz">Pays de Retz</a>. He was murdered in 857 by his cousin Salomon, who took the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erispoe.jpg" alt="Erispoe" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moreau.henri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:241_%C3%8Ele-aux-Moines.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Brittany, the Armorican peninsula settled by migrants from south-western Britain in the fifth and sixth centuries, had formed a kingdom under Nominoe, <b>Erispoe</b> and Salomon in the ninth century, when its rulers fought the Carolingians and won the counties of Rennes and Nantes.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Duchy of Brittany · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Near Grand-Fougeray on the border of Brittany, the Breton army of <b>Erispoe</b> defeated the West Frankish king Charles the Bald.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-22">22 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 9th century Cornouaille was drawn into the unified Kingdom of Brittany under Nominoe and <b>Erispoe</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/cornouaille">Cornouaille</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 9th century Domnonée was absorbed into the Kingdom of Brittany created by Nominoe and <b>Erispoe</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/domnonee">Domnonée</a></li><li><blockquote>His son <b>Erispoe</b> won again at Jengland in 851, and the Treaty of Angers recognised him as king with Rennes, Nantes and the Pays de Retz.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-brittany">Kingdom of Brittany</a></li></ul></section>
